WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.734
"Which NAD+ Booster Is Best?"

00:00:07.257 --> 00:00:11.200
So, which NAD+ boosting
supplement is best?

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.920
There’s no clear standout,

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.680
as hardly any of the preclinical
effects found in the lab

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.800
have translated into evidence
of human clinical benefit.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.080
Perhaps, this failure is to be expected
given the complexity of NAD+ physiology,

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:30.360
with its juggling of multiple precursors,
production pathways, and recycling routes.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.560
The bottom line is that it’s just too early
to say if NAD+ booster supplementation

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:38.160
will ever live up to even
a fraction of the hype.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.600
Many more, larger, and longer-term studies
are necessary to establish safety and efficacy.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.760
The problem is that because NA, NAM,
NR, and NMN are all natural products,

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.280
they can’t be patented;

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.560
so, the money for well-designed
clinical trials is not as available.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.000
The reason there have been comparatively
more trials done on NR than NMN

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.120
is that patents were originally issued for NR
before being invalidated as unpatentable.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.240
Perhaps blindly overloading the
system with NAD+ precursors

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.680
is not the best way to go
about NAD+ restoration.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:21.080
The body seems too smart to allow such
blunt incursion to affect tissue levels.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.000
Maybe these supplements are
just profit-making distractions

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.360
from more natural approaches.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.520
Broadly, there are three main
ways to increase NAD+ levels.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.640
Increasing the supply of NAD+
precursors is just the first.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.640
The other two are having
the body make more,

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.120
by activating NAD+
synthesizing enzymes,

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:48.560
or have the body use less, via an
inhibition of excess NAD+ degradation.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:54.880
The primary determinant of NAD+
synthesis in the enzyme NAMPT.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.280
An abundance of NAMPT tends to
decrease with age in human muscle,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.280
dropping steadily by about 40%
between the ages of 20 and 80.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.880
In our liver, it drops by half.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.000
However, age-related diseases,
such as atherosclerosis,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.760
cancer, diabetes,
and rheumatoid arthritis,

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.440
have been found to exacerbate
NAMPT decline,

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:17.080
raising a chicken or
the egg question.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.360
There’s where interventional
trials come in.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:25.000
Similar NAMPT declines have been
noted in aging rats and mice.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.760
Does boosting NAMPT help?

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.960
Increasing NAMPT or its species
equivalent increases the lifespans

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.360
of yeast, fruit flies, and rodents.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:41.080
An NAMPT boost also increases aerobic
capacity and exercise endurance in mice,

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:44.040
in addition to helping them live longer.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.800
Enhanced expression of NAMPT increases
the NAD+ levels in the muscles in mice

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.120
comparable to feeding them
dietary NAD+ precursors,

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:53.880
but if you remember,

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.920
NAD+ precursors don’t seem to be able to
affect NAD+ muscle levels in most people.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.400
In fact, such supplements can
actually suppress NAMPT,

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.880
while boosting that methylating enzyme
to rid the body of the excess.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.840
In addition to methyl depletion,

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.720
chronic administration
of these supplements

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.880
could potentially then leave people
worse off should they ever stop them.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:19.720
There is, however, a way to naturally
boost NAMPT and NAD+ levels in humans

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.720
without any supplements: exercise.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.640
Athletes have about twice the NAMPT
expression in their musculature

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.880
compared to sedentary individuals.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.800
To prove cause and effect,

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.480
sedentary men and women started
a stationary bike exercise protocol,

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.800
and within three weeks, NAMPT
levels increased by 127%.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.480
Resistance training can
also increase NAMPT,

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.360
and this can also translate into a
127% increase in muscle NAD+ levels

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.120
and a rise in sirtuin activity.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.080
In other words,

00:03:54.080 --> 00:04:00.243
exercise can do what NAD+
boosting supplements can’t.

